{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1356645-unchained-in-manch-vegas-alan-thorn-prologue","id":1356645,"title":"Unchained in Manch-Vegas: Alan Thorn - Prologue","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-23T08:05:59-08:00","id":1356645,"title":"Unchained in Manch-Vegas: Alan Thorn - Prologue","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I only had one player show up this weekend, so I decided to do a one-shot of their Fall from being an angel.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cast:</span></span></b><ul><li><b>Alan Thorn</b> - Psychopomp. Works as a Programmer for a startup tech company.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Session Report</b><br /> <br /> Alan Thorn\u2019s first moment of existence was a voice in his head, \u201cMake sure Analytical United Global\u2019s quantum computer is operational at 10 years. Defend the project from any sabotage.\u201d Alan arrived with a ringing telephone in a British phone booth in the middle of Manchester, NH. He had a suitcase and his mission.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">He arrived at the A.U.G. offices in the millyard. The front desk did not have any record of an interview that day. For an Angel, that was a slight inconvenience, the company did have an opening for a quantum computing expert. The CEO Jaymes apologized to Alan and showed him around. The God-Machine provided Alan with a piece of infrastructure in the disguise of a backup server in the server room.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Over the next month Alan had to keep IT from checking on that particular server. He didn\u2019t want to have to deal with any Mortals becoming Stigmatics. But two months in, there was a cyber-attack, a virus managed to bypass the A.U.G. firewall. He managed to track the attack to a cyber-cafe in the city. After a little hunting he found a stout woman wearing a black bowler hat. She claimed to have authorization to probe A.U.G.\u2019s network. The paperwork checked out, but Alan was not convinced. He gave her back a USB stick with a tracking virus on it. It ended up infecting the cyber-cafe computers, but it did give him backdoor access to their webcams.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Later that week Jaymes pressed him to show some progress on the project, negotiating for more equipment and monetary investment Alan was able to secure at least some of Jaymes confidence that they will be the first out on the market. But when he got to his desk he found a letter with a black hat emblem on it. \u201cNice trick with the virus. Your quantum computer will never be finished.\u201d The paper had a printer ID number that Alan managed to track down to a print shop nearby. The hacker was sloppy, she had used a credit card. He got to her apartment and used his twilight form to investigate. The door was wired to explode if anyone opened it. He downloaded schematics for a 10 year plan to destroy the computer and relocated the explosive to the window where the hacker would likely enter. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">He waited and the hacker did appear climbing up the fire escape ready to fall into his trap. The explosive went off, but the hacker only suffered minor injury. Using his powers, Alan caused a car to slam into the woman. She knew what was happening and she ran down an alley. Alan materialized and tried to slam her head in with lead pipe. But she had disappeared, he called her cellphone and he heard the ringer coming from a homeless man sleeping in the alley. He slammed Alan against a wall and threw a floppy disk at him, his bane, burning his face. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The demon had escaped. But Alan knew what he had to do. The occult matrix was at risk, the time table needed to be moved up so the demonic hacker couldn\u2019t sabotage it. He built the quantum computer, and what should have taken 10 years was done within 6 months. And the God-Machine was displeased and Alan fell from grace.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b><br /> This helped me really get an idea for what Alan Thorn is like as well as establishing his rivalry with the Demon Blackhat.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}